  "query_preview": "..\nCurrent visible satellite imagery depicts the Marianas in a dry, \ndiffusive pattern following a very weak trade-wind trough \ndownstream. Earlier this morning, small areas of moderate convection\nand isolated thunderstorms were seen far NE of Saipan and ESE of \nGuam. However, both areas have been reduced to lingering cirrus, \nsupporting the isolated shower regime at least through tonight. Due \nto the slowing and divergence of the overall surface flow, winds \nwill become light and variable tonight, returning to the usual 10 to \n15 mph easterly trades shortly after sunrise. This pattern will \npersist through at least midweek. Forecaster confidence is still low \nregarding Invest 92W (see Tropical Systems section below) as the \ndifferent model groups disagree from each other. Therefore, PoPs were\nkept at 30 percent for the last few periods of the forecast. Whether\nor not this system impacts the Marianas will greatly depend on its \nevolution for the next several days.",
